    skos:prefLabel "Invasive ungulates pollute wetlands in Australia’s Northern Territory; and indigenous rangers document the impacts on water quality and cultural species, including Nymphaea spp. (water lilies)." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/IAS23-Figure4.44> a ipbes:Figure,
        ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:SubChapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/IAS23-4.5> ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Spodoptera frugiperda negatively impacts crop yields, income and production costs, food security, health and livestock feed availability (x axis). The results are presented in percentages of the 33 case studies reviewed. A data management report for the literature review underpinning this figure is available at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5760266 The synthetic pesticides used by smallholders for Spodoptera frugiperda control have been shown to pose high risks to human health (Murray et al., 2019, 2021; Kumela et al., 2019). Several studies have shown that farmers who used pesticide to control Spodoptera frugiperda experience pesticide-related" ;
    ipbes:hasDoi "10.5281/zenodo.8046326" ;
    dcterms:identifier "Figure4.44" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Percentage of documented impacts (y axis) of Spodoptera frugiperda (fall armyworm) on good quality of life of Indigenous Peoples and local communities." .

